From 532a6fc250e0b134444d068dff5f9f326d7d05ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:41:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chat, sampling: K2-Horizon official weights: tool call in
 reasoning, repeated open tag, empty first-token stop

Root causes (official IFM K2-Horizon-7B Q4_K_M, fleet 2026-09-26, opencode via
LiteLLM), after the template's "<ifm|think_faster>\n" generation prompt:
- the model sometimes emits "<ifm|tool_calls>..." without closing the reasoning
  (8/42 opencode-shaped runs); the parser stayed in reasoning, the whole call
  became reasoning_content, finish=stop, and the client ended the turn.
- it sometimes repeats the open tag ("<ifm|think>\n</ifm|think>...", 4/42);
  the parser only knew the effort's own start tag, so "<ifm|think>" leaked
  into reasoning_content.
- it can emit an EOG token (id 1 / 250019) as its very first token (4-12% at
  temp 1 after an empty assistant turn in the history): a 1-token empty stop.

Fix: analyze_reasoning::start_alts (redundant open tags consumed) and
implicit_ends_with_tools (<ifm|tool_calls> ends the reasoning when tools are
offered); an empty-reply guard sampler (common_sampler::eguard, request field
no_empty_reply_inert) masks EOG until something besides whitespace/reasoning
tags was generated. Streaming and non-streaming share the one PEG parser.

Verification (42 runs per row, stream + non-stream, low effort, 3080 Ti):
official file before 13 leaks / 9 tool calls stuck in reasoning / 9 empty
stops; after 0 / 0 / 0. Community quant before: 15 / 4 / 4 (same quirks, so
model behaviour, not a weights regression). Guard at /completion level: 6-12
EOG-first of 100 before, 0 of 100 after. test-chat gets real-output cases that
fail before and pass after; ctest -L main (58) and -R split-balance pass.
FLEET.md documents the mechanism and the (identical) GGUF metadata/template.

